WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.066 --> 00:00:00.667
Former President

00:00:00.667 --> 00:00:01.501
Trump claiming

00:00:01.501 --> 00:00:04.170
he knows nothing about a 20, 21 meeting.

00:00:04.604 --> 00:00:06.473
Federal prosecutors have on tape.

00:00:06.473 --> 00:00:07.607
CNN reports that Trump

00:00:07.607 --> 00:00:08.842
acknowledged in the meeting

00:00:08.842 --> 00:00:10.176
at his New Jersey golf club

00:00:10.176 --> 00:00:11.211
he still has

00:00:11.211 --> 00:00:13.380
a classified Pentagon document

00:00:13.380 --> 00:00:16.383
about a potential attack plan on Iran.

00:00:16.950 --> 00:00:20.587
This was his denial last night on Fox

00:00:20.587 --> 00:00:21.721
You know, I don't know anything about it.

00:00:21.721 --> 00:00:22.322
All I know is,

00:00:22.322 --> 00:00:24.424
is everything I did was right.

00:00:24.724 --> 00:00:26.526
We have the Presidential Records Act,

00:00:26.526 --> 00:00:28.828
which I abided by 100%.

00:00:28.828 --> 00:00:30.163
It's a continuation

00:00:30.163 --> 00:00:31.898
of the greatest witch hunt of all time.

00:00:31.898 --> 00:00:32.966
It's a hoax.

00:00:32.966 --> 00:00:35.168
And it has to do

00:00:36.136 --> 00:00:38.271
It has to do

00:00:38.271 --> 00:00:39.572
more than anything else

00:00:39.572 --> 00:00:40.974
with trying to interfere

00:00:40.974 --> 00:00:42.642
with the election.

00:00:42.675 --> 00:00:43.710
For more on the meeting

00:00:43.710 --> 00:00:45.612
and the federal investigation,

00:00:45.612 --> 00:00:46.813
let's turn to CNN's

00:00:46.813 --> 00:00:48.148
Paula Reid in Washington.

00:00:50.283 --> 00:00:50.750
Former

00:00:50.750 --> 00:00:51.951
President Donald Trump

00:00:51.951 --> 00:00:53.820
campaigning in Iowa,

00:00:53.820 --> 00:00:55.889
refusing to take questions

00:00:55.889 --> 00:00:57.991
on the bombshell revelation

00:00:57.991 --> 00:01:00.060
he was recorded discussing

00:01:00.060 --> 00:01:01.761
classified information.

00:01:01.761 --> 00:01:02.062
Mr.

00:01:02.062 --> 00:01:03.630
President, why did you take classified

00:01:03.630 --> 00:01:05.231
documents concerning General

00:01:05.231 --> 00:01:07.100
but continued to claim

00:01:07.100 --> 00:01:09.602
he's a victim of federal investigators?

00:01:09.903 --> 00:01:10.837
I'm a victim of it.

00:01:10.837 --> 00:01:11.771
They've come after me.

00:01:11.771 --> 00:01:13.740
They've come after me on many things.

00:01:13.740 --> 00:01:16.810
I wrote this after CNN's exclusive

00:01:16.810 --> 00:01:18.678
reporting that prosecutors

00:01:18.678 --> 00:01:20.947
now have an audio recording of Trump

00:01:20.947 --> 00:01:23.016
talking about a classified plan

00:01:23.016 --> 00:01:24.651
to invade Iran

00:01:24.651 --> 00:01:27.087
while he was at his Bedminster Golf Club.

00:01:27.253 --> 00:01:29.589
Months after he left the White House.

00:01:29.889 --> 00:01:30.557
Among those

00:01:30.557 --> 00:01:31.791
attending the meeting,

00:01:31.791 --> 00:01:33.226
several Trump aides

00:01:33.226 --> 00:01:34.360
and two people

00:01:34.360 --> 00:01:36.429
working on an autobiography

00:01:36.429 --> 00:01:38.465
for former White House chief of staff

00:01:38.465 --> 00:01:39.833
Mark Meadows.

00:01:39.833 --> 00:01:42.268
None of them had security clearances.

00:01:42.535 --> 00:01:44.637
During this time, Trump had aides

00:01:44.637 --> 00:01:46.239
record his conversation

00:01:46.239 --> 00:01:48.274
with journalists and writers.

00:01:48.274 --> 00:01:50.910
They became automatically declassified

00:01:50.910 --> 00:01:51.678
when I took them.

00:01:51.678 --> 00:01:52.178
Trump,

00:01:52.178 --> 00:01:54.147
under investigation for his handling

00:01:54.147 --> 00:01:56.116
of national security secrets,

00:01:56.116 --> 00:01:57.784
has previously insisted

00:01:57.784 --> 00:01:59.252
that he declassified

00:01:59.252 --> 00:02:01.821
any sensitive material in his possession.

00:02:01.921 --> 00:02:02.622
If you're the president

00:02:02.622 --> 00:02:03.623
of the United States,

00:02:03.623 --> 00:02:05.658
you can declassify just by saying

00:02:05.658 --> 00:02:06.593
it's declassified.

00:02:06.593 --> 00:02:08.094
Even by thinking about it

00:02:08.094 --> 00:02:08.795
But sources

00:02:08.795 --> 00:02:09.762
tell CNN

00:02:09.762 --> 00:02:11.164
on this recording,

00:02:11.164 --> 00:02:13.600
Trump claims to still be in possession

00:02:13.600 --> 00:02:16.169
of a Pentagon document, suggests

00:02:16.202 --> 00:02:17.670
he would like to share it.

00:02:17.670 --> 00:02:18.872
And then acknowledges

00:02:18.872 --> 00:02:20.473
the limits of his ability

00:02:20.473 --> 00:02:21.841
to declassify it.

00:02:21.841 --> 00:02:24.777
All of this undercutting his own defense.

00:02:25.078 --> 00:02:25.545
Asked

00:02:25.545 --> 00:02:26.579
if he had ever shared

00:02:26.579 --> 00:02:29.115
any information at CNN's town hall.

00:02:29.315 --> 00:02:31.217
Not really. I would have the right to.

00:02:31.217 --> 00:02:32.785
By the way, they would dismiss if I did.

00:02:33.853 --> 00:02:35.221
Not that I can think of.

00:02:35.221 --> 00:02:36.422
Let me just tell you,

00:02:36.422 --> 00:02:37.423
I have the absolute right

00:02:37.423 --> 00:02:38.858
to do whatever I want with them.

00:02:38.858 --> 00:02:41.161
This summer, 20, 21 recording

00:02:41.394 --> 00:02:42.662
comes out of Trump's

00:02:42.662 --> 00:02:44.430
New Jersey golf club.

00:02:44.430 --> 00:02:44.998
It's now

00:02:44.998 --> 00:02:46.833
the second confirmed state

00:02:46.833 --> 00:02:49.269
where he has had classified information

00:02:49.402 --> 00:02:50.837
after the FBI walked

00:02:50.837 --> 00:02:52.005
out of his Mar-A-Lago

00:02:52.005 --> 00:02:53.239
estate in Florida

00:02:53.239 --> 00:02:55.875
with boxes of top secret documents.

00:02:56.309 --> 00:02:58.912
The Trump campaign saying the DOJ's

00:02:58.912 --> 00:03:00.313
continued interference

00:03:00.313 --> 00:03:01.181
in the presidential

00:03:01.181 --> 00:03:02.715
election is shameful

00:03:02.715 --> 00:03:04.751
and this meritless investigation

00:03:04.984 --> 00:03:06.452
should cease wasting

00:03:06.452 --> 00:03:08.054
the American taxpayer's money

00:03:08.054 --> 00:03:10.256
on Democrat political objectives.

00:03:10.356 --> 00:03:11.624
When we searched Bedminster,

00:03:11.624 --> 00:03:13.193
there were no classified documents

00:03:13.193 --> 00:03:14.360
or marked documents there.

00:03:14.360 --> 00:03:15.495
Former Trump lawyer

00:03:15.495 --> 00:03:16.863
Tim Latorre,

00:03:16.863 --> 00:03:17.931
who left Trump's

00:03:17.931 --> 00:03:18.565
legal team

00:03:18.565 --> 00:03:19.632
in recent weeks,

00:03:19.632 --> 00:03:21.301
says the classification

00:03:21.301 --> 00:03:22.735
status of the document

00:03:22.735 --> 00:03:23.436
Trump is heard

00:03:23.436 --> 00:03:25.572
talking about is irrelevant

00:03:25.572 --> 00:03:26.706
based on the laws

00:03:26.706 --> 00:03:28.575
that are cited in the search warrant

00:03:28.575 --> 00:03:30.276
that was executed in summer.

00:03:30.276 --> 00:03:31.644
20, 22.

00:03:31.644 --> 00:03:33.813
Really, what DOJ is investigating

00:03:33.813 --> 00:03:35.615
is willful retention

00:03:35.615 --> 00:03:37.951
of national defense information,

00:03:37.951 --> 00:03:40.119
whether it's classified or declassified,

00:03:40.186 --> 00:03:42.355
is not an element of that offense.

00:03:42.388 --> 00:03:43.189
Former President

00:03:43.189 --> 00:03:45.291
Trump's lawyers have asked for a meeting

00:03:45.291 --> 00:03:47.227
with Attorney General Merrick Garland

00:03:47.227 --> 00:03:49.095
to express their concerns

00:03:49.095 --> 00:03:50.363
about the special counsel's

00:03:50.363 --> 00:03:51.864
investigation.

00:03:51.864 --> 00:03:52.899
But one of Trump's attorneys

00:03:52.899 --> 00:03:53.666
tells CNN

00:03:53.666 --> 00:03:55.468
there have been some communications

00:03:55.468 --> 00:03:56.669
between DOJ

00:03:56.669 --> 00:03:58.004
and the Trump legal team

00:03:58.004 --> 00:04:00.206
about the possibility of this meeting.

00:04:00.506 --> 00:04:01.741
But the fact that there is this

00:04:01.741 --> 00:04:04.711
recording in the hands of investigators

00:04:04.744 --> 00:04:05.845
really undercuts

00:04:05.845 --> 00:04:07.113
their key concern,

00:04:07.113 --> 00:04:08.281
which is an allegation

00:04:08.281 --> 00:04:08.881
that this is just

00:04:08.881 --> 00:04:11.451
a politically motivated investigation.

00:04:11.718 --> 00:04:13.620
But if they do get this meeting

00:04:13.620 --> 00:04:14.587
with the attorney general

00:04:14.587 --> 00:04:15.655
or some other Justice

00:04:15.655 --> 00:04:16.923
Department official,

00:04:16.923 --> 00:04:19.025
they will clearly have much to discuss.

00:04:19.559 --> 00:04:21.728
Polaroid, CNN, Washington.

00:04:22.028 --> 00:04:24.364
The GOP field of candidates is growing

00:04:24.364 --> 00:04:26.232
and it's about to get even bigger.

00:04:26.232 --> 00:04:27.667
CNN's Jeff Zeleny live in Des

00:04:27.667 --> 00:04:28.668
Moines, Iowa, this morning.

00:04:28.668 --> 00:04:29.202
Jeff,

00:04:29.435 --> 00:04:30.169
where President Trump

00:04:30.169 --> 00:04:31.504
was campaigning in Iowa

00:04:31.504 --> 00:04:32.071
yesterday

00:04:32.071 --> 00:04:34.140
and talked about his competitors.

00:04:34.140 --> 00:04:35.141
How does he see the field

00:04:37.810 --> 00:04:38.478
Hey, good morning.

00:04:38.478 --> 00:04:39.779
How the field is getting bigger

00:04:39.779 --> 00:04:40.747
in next week alone.

00:04:40.747 --> 00:04:42.248
Three Republican candidates

00:04:42.248 --> 00:04:43.783
are set to join the race.

00:04:43.783 --> 00:04:45.785
In fact, there are so many alternatives

00:04:45.952 --> 00:04:47.086
to Donald Trump.

00:04:47.086 --> 00:04:49.289
It is benefiting one person of all.

00:04:49.289 --> 00:04:50.623
And that's the former president,

00:04:50.623 --> 00:04:52.725
which is exactly what he's counting on.

00:04:53.660 --> 00:04:54.661
And we presume

00:04:54.661 --> 00:04:55.295
so far,

00:04:55.295 --> 00:04:56.729
Donald Trump is getting most

00:04:56.729 --> 00:04:57.930
everything he wanted from

00:04:57.930 --> 00:04:59.932
the Republican presidential campaign.

00:04:59.932 --> 00:05:01.401
There's no way I can lose Iowa.

00:05:01.401 --> 00:05:02.435
Let's see what happens.

00:05:02.435 --> 00:05:03.936
I don't think so.

00:05:03.936 --> 00:05:05.238
We'd have to

00:05:05.238 --> 00:05:07.473
we'd have to do some really bad things

00:05:07.473 --> 00:05:08.508
to lose at this point,

00:05:08.508 --> 00:05:09.876
including a list of rivals

00:05:09.876 --> 00:05:11.344
that's growing by the week

00:05:11.344 --> 00:05:12.178
with the anyone

00:05:12.178 --> 00:05:12.612
but Trump

00:05:12.612 --> 00:05:13.613
lane of the race

00:05:13.613 --> 00:05:15.381
becoming remarkably crowded

00:05:15.381 --> 00:05:17.016
I think it's advantageous to Trump.

00:05:17.016 --> 00:05:17.884
I don't like that.

00:05:17.884 --> 00:05:19.919
Julie Marla is a loyal Republican

00:05:19.919 --> 00:05:21.521
who came to see Florida Governor Ron

00:05:21.521 --> 00:05:22.822
DeSantis the other night

00:05:22.822 --> 00:05:24.924
and is sizing up several contenders.

00:05:24.924 --> 00:05:26.959
But she offered pointed words of advice

00:05:26.959 --> 00:05:28.528
for those entering the race.

00:05:28.528 --> 00:05:30.596
Stay for a while and see what happens,

00:05:30.596 --> 00:05:32.732
but then don't stay too long

00:05:32.732 --> 00:05:34.500
because we need

00:05:34.500 --> 00:05:35.835
we need to face the Democrats.

00:05:35.835 --> 00:05:36.936
As summer approaches,

00:05:36.936 --> 00:05:38.538
the Republican field is starting

00:05:38.538 --> 00:05:40.039
to burst at the seams,

00:05:40.039 --> 00:05:41.240
with former Vice President

00:05:41.240 --> 00:05:43.376
Mike Pence and former New Jersey Governor

00:05:43.376 --> 00:05:45.511
Chris Christie set to jump in next week,

00:05:45.511 --> 00:05:46.913
joining former Governor Nikki

00:05:46.913 --> 00:05:47.947
Haley and Senator Tim

00:05:47.947 --> 00:05:49.382
Scott of South Carolina.

00:05:49.382 --> 00:05:50.283
Former Arkansas

00:05:50.283 --> 00:05:50.917
Governor Asa

00:05:50.917 --> 00:05:52.352
Hutchinson and entrepreneur

00:05:52.352 --> 00:05:53.553
Vivek Ramaswamy,

00:05:53.553 --> 00:05:55.221
who are already in the race.

00:05:55.221 --> 00:05:55.822
North Dakota

00:05:55.822 --> 00:05:57.690
Governor Doug Burgum is also poised

00:05:57.690 --> 00:05:58.825
to announce next week.

00:05:58.825 --> 00:05:59.492
And New Hampshire

00:05:59.492 --> 00:06:00.093
Governor Chris

00:06:00.093 --> 00:06:02.228
Sununu promises a decision soon.

00:06:02.228 --> 00:06:02.995
And Virginia

00:06:02.995 --> 00:06:03.563
Governor Glenn

00:06:03.563 --> 00:06:05.531
Youngkin is not ruling out a run later

00:06:05.531 --> 00:06:06.332
this year.

00:06:06.332 --> 00:06:08.701
If some contenders flame out, well,

00:06:08.701 --> 00:06:09.602
if that many candidates

00:06:09.602 --> 00:06:11.971
stay in the race that benefits Trump,

00:06:11.971 --> 00:06:14.240
Trump will win by the power division

00:06:14.240 --> 00:06:14.741
And that's

00:06:14.741 --> 00:06:15.842
why we'll see

00:06:15.842 --> 00:06:17.410
if we learned our lesson,

00:06:17.410 --> 00:06:18.644
learned our lesson well.

00:06:18.644 --> 00:06:19.278
Bob Vander

00:06:19.278 --> 00:06:21.080
Plaats, an influential evangelical

00:06:21.080 --> 00:06:22.081
leader in Iowa,

00:06:22.081 --> 00:06:23.449
said the party should not repeat

00:06:23.449 --> 00:06:25.218
the mistakes of 2016

00:06:25.218 --> 00:06:26.652
when Trump claimed the nomination

00:06:26.652 --> 00:06:28.621
with a divided Republican electorate,

00:06:28.621 --> 00:06:30.089
rather than facing a head to head

00:06:30.089 --> 00:06:32.091
match with one strong opponent.

00:06:32.091 --> 00:06:34.227
So my concern is so how many get in?

00:06:34.327 --> 00:06:36.662
It's when do they get out and win?

00:06:37.230 --> 00:06:38.464
And when do they give America

00:06:38.464 --> 00:06:39.298
a clear choice

00:06:39.298 --> 00:06:41.000
between the former president

00:06:41.000 --> 00:06:42.602
and an alternative,

00:06:42.602 --> 00:06:44.170
a big field is precisely

00:06:44.170 --> 00:06:46.839
what Trump is banking on and basking in.

00:06:46.839 --> 00:06:47.940
As he shook hands

00:06:47.940 --> 00:06:48.841
and took questions

00:06:48.841 --> 00:06:51.077
at a series of small events in Iowa

00:06:51.077 --> 00:06:51.944
while making clear

00:06:51.944 --> 00:06:54.981
he's fixated on one rival above all Iran,

00:06:55.081 --> 00:06:57.083
as I call him Ron to sanctimonious,

00:06:57.183 --> 00:06:57.583
the former

00:06:57.583 --> 00:06:59.519
president seized upon a leading argument

00:06:59.519 --> 00:07:01.621
DeSantis made to voters here this week.

00:07:01.687 --> 00:07:04.323
We could bring back George Washington.

00:07:04.357 --> 00:07:05.224
I don't know that

00:07:05.224 --> 00:07:06.826
he would be able to get it done in

00:07:06.826 --> 00:07:07.860
just four years

00:07:07.860 --> 00:07:08.795
and sought to mock

00:07:08.795 --> 00:07:10.029
the Florida governor's pitch

00:07:10.029 --> 00:07:11.898
that he's eligible for two terms,

00:07:11.898 --> 00:07:13.699
not simply one more like Trump.

00:07:13.699 --> 00:07:14.667
You'll need eight years.

00:07:14.667 --> 00:07:15.568
You need six months.

00:07:15.568 --> 00:07:17.837
We can turn this thing around so quickly.

00:07:17.837 --> 00:07:19.839
Who the hell wants to wait eight years?

00:07:19.839 --> 00:07:21.207
You don't need eight years.

00:07:21.207 --> 00:07:22.675
And in New Hampshire Thursday,

00:07:22.675 --> 00:07:24.477
two centers hitting back at Trump.

00:07:24.477 --> 00:07:26.379
Why didn't he do it his first four years?

00:07:26.379 --> 00:07:27.914
As the campaign intensifies,

00:07:27.914 --> 00:07:28.981
signs are emerging

00:07:28.981 --> 00:07:30.049
that it's far too early

00:07:30.049 --> 00:07:31.984
to presume it's a two man contest.

00:07:31.984 --> 00:07:33.085
As candidates begin

00:07:33.085 --> 00:07:34.053
blanketing the state

00:07:34.053 --> 00:07:34.587
that begins

00:07:34.587 --> 00:07:36.355
the Republican nomination battle early

00:07:36.355 --> 00:07:37.156
next year.

00:07:37.156 --> 00:07:38.891
Laurie Hartson also believes

00:07:38.891 --> 00:07:40.793
the field is cluttered in her mind.

00:07:40.793 --> 00:07:42.562
It's already a one man race

00:07:42.562 --> 00:07:44.230
President Trump already made

00:07:44.230 --> 00:07:45.631
America great.

00:07:45.631 --> 00:07:47.767
Now we need him back to fix it.

00:07:47.800 --> 00:07:48.901
She drove 4 hours

00:07:48.901 --> 00:07:49.669
to catch a glimpse

00:07:49.669 --> 00:07:50.636
of the former president

00:07:50.636 --> 00:07:52.572
outside one of his Iowa stops.

00:07:52.572 --> 00:07:53.339
Do you think that others

00:07:53.339 --> 00:07:54.841
should step aside

00:07:54.841 --> 00:07:55.875
and let him run

00:07:55.875 --> 00:07:57.477
and focus on President Biden?

00:07:57.477 --> 00:07:59.011
Or do you think a competitive Republican

00:07:59.011 --> 00:08:01.514
primary is fine, let you leave?

00:08:01.981 --> 00:08:03.683
I wish they would step aside,

00:08:03.683 --> 00:08:05.518
but they won't.

00:08:05.518 --> 00:08:08.354
And I don't know if it's ego they want.

00:08:08.354 --> 00:08:10.256
And Mark him coming

00:08:10.256 --> 00:08:10.790
in, it's like,

00:08:10.790 --> 00:08:12.558
come on, Mike Pence, really?

00:08:12.558 --> 00:08:13.593
Mike, give it up.

00:08:16.629 --> 00:08:17.096
So that

00:08:17.096 --> 00:08:17.630
sentiment, of

00:08:17.630 --> 00:08:18.397
course, is

00:08:18.397 --> 00:08:20.700
expressing the challenges facing

00:08:20.700 --> 00:08:21.234
former Vice

00:08:21.234 --> 00:08:22.268
President Mike Pence

00:08:22.268 --> 00:08:25.004
as he announces his bid here in Iowa.

00:08:25.004 --> 00:08:25.838
Next week.

00:08:25.838 --> 00:08:27.106
There are also many Republicans

00:08:27.106 --> 00:08:28.374
we've spoken to who

00:08:28.374 --> 00:08:30.743
welcome his true conservative views.

00:08:30.743 --> 00:08:32.211
And he also is reaching out

00:08:32.211 --> 00:08:33.946
to evangelical voters

00:08:33.946 --> 00:08:34.547
who are, of course,

00:08:34.547 --> 00:08:36.249
very important to this core.

00:08:36.249 --> 00:08:37.550
So we're virtually

00:08:37.550 --> 00:08:38.451
all of the candidates

00:08:38.451 --> 00:08:39.252
back in Iowa

00:08:39.252 --> 00:08:39.852
this weekend,

00:08:39.852 --> 00:08:41.787
with the exception of Donald Trump.

00:08:41.787 --> 00:08:42.355
They have an event

00:08:42.355 --> 00:08:43.556
at the Iowa State Fairgrounds.

00:08:43.556 --> 00:08:44.790
So Republican voters

00:08:44.790 --> 00:08:46.826
have many options to choose.

00:08:47.159 --> 00:08:48.261
And that is specifically

00:08:48.261 --> 00:08:48.761
what worries

00:08:48.761 --> 00:08:49.629
some of the voters

00:08:49.629 --> 00:08:51.731
who are looking to turn the page.

00:08:52.031 --> 00:08:53.299
Well, Jeff, it's interesting

00:08:53.299 --> 00:08:54.367
because you say in your piece

00:08:54.367 --> 00:08:54.634
you know,

00:08:54.634 --> 00:08:56.202
it may be too early to say

00:08:56.202 --> 00:08:57.904
it's a two man race.

00:08:57.904 --> 00:08:58.504
Walk us through

00:08:58.504 --> 00:08:59.639
some of these other candidates,

00:08:59.639 --> 00:09:00.306
because I think there

00:09:00.306 --> 00:09:01.073
is this question

00:09:01.073 --> 00:09:01.707
about do

00:09:01.707 --> 00:09:02.642
any of the other candidates

00:09:02.642 --> 00:09:04.443
have a real shot

00:09:04.443 --> 00:09:06.279
other than Trump and DeSantis

00:09:08.614 --> 00:09:08.881
Sure.

00:09:08.881 --> 00:09:10.716
That's what the campaign is all about.

00:09:10.716 --> 00:09:11.751
And here

00:09:11.751 --> 00:09:13.452
we're just the beginning of June.

00:09:13.452 --> 00:09:15.087
The candidates who are out working,

00:09:15.087 --> 00:09:17.223
talking to voters, Nikki Haley, for one,

00:09:17.223 --> 00:09:18.391
she's been having more events

00:09:18.391 --> 00:09:18.858
here in Iowa,

00:09:18.858 --> 00:09:20.693
the former South Carolina governor,

00:09:20.693 --> 00:09:21.894
than virtually any other candidate.

00:09:21.894 --> 00:09:23.796
She's gaining a bit of traction.

00:09:23.796 --> 00:09:25.831
South Carolina Senator Tim Scott.

00:09:25.831 --> 00:09:27.733
His name comes up again and again

00:09:27.733 --> 00:09:28.801
and he has a lot of money

00:09:28.801 --> 00:09:30.102
behind his candidacy.

00:09:30.102 --> 00:09:31.237
He's already

00:09:31.237 --> 00:09:32.371
running television

00:09:32.371 --> 00:09:34.140
ads here on the air in Iowa.

00:09:34.140 --> 00:09:34.607
So, look,

00:09:34.607 --> 00:09:37.944
this is the season of where voters are

00:09:39.378 --> 00:09:41.047
are shopping, if you will, looking at all

00:09:41.047 --> 00:09:42.248
these potential candidates.

00:09:42.248 --> 00:09:44.317
And yes, Trump is leading the race.

00:09:44.317 --> 00:09:45.451
He is the leading candidate,

00:09:45.451 --> 00:09:47.453
but he's not the presumptive nominee.

00:09:47.453 --> 00:09:48.988
It is far too soon to say that.

00:09:48.988 --> 00:09:50.122
One thing about Iowa.

00:09:50.122 --> 00:09:50.723
The history of it

00:09:50.723 --> 00:09:52.959
shows that the frontrunners are often

00:09:52.959 --> 00:09:54.226
humbled here.

00:09:54.226 --> 00:09:54.694
Many people

00:09:54.694 --> 00:09:56.762
who come into Iowa back in 2008

00:09:56.762 --> 00:09:58.464
for example, Rudy Giuliani,

00:09:58.464 --> 00:09:59.565
he was seen as a frontrunner.

00:09:59.565 --> 00:10:00.833
Of course, he fizzled.

00:10:00.833 --> 00:10:02.034
The list of that is long.

00:10:02.034 --> 00:10:02.768
So the state is known

00:10:02.768 --> 00:10:05.037
for elevating challengers.

00:10:05.037 --> 00:10:06.672
Humbling frontrunners.

00:10:06.672 --> 00:10:08.507
We will see what happens this time.

00:10:08.507 --> 00:10:10.142
That is a very interesting

00:10:10.142 --> 00:10:11.110
historical nugget.

00:10:11.110 --> 00:10:12.478
Jeff Zeleny, thank you.

